          "path": "_m/g/c/x/7/sheriff-hutton-castle-wp/hbr-scaffolding-covers-the-sw-.jpg",
          "filename": "HBR Scaffolding covers the SW Tower - geograph.org.uk - 1226850.jpg",
          "caption": "HBR Scaffolding covers the SW Tower Repointing and weatherproofing the remains of Sheriff Hutton Castle. Built by John Lord Neville in 1382, it is almost an exact copy of Bolton Castle (in Wensleydale), it later belonged to Richard III and to Henry Fitzroy, Duke of Richmond. It began to decay in 1547 and by 1625 it had been removed of its floors &amp; roofs, although a 15thC range in the outer court long remained in use as a farmhouse.",
          "alt": "HBR Scaffolding covers the SW Tower Repointing and weatherproofing the remains of Sheriff Hutton Castle. Built by John Lord Neville in 1382, it is almost an exact copy of Bolton Castle (in Wensleydale), it later belonged to Richard III and to Henry Fitzroy, Duke of Richmond. It began to decay in 1547 and by 1625 it had been removed of its floors &amp; roofs, although a 15thC range in the outer court long remained in use as a farmhouse.",
          "width": 640,
